@echo off
rem ---------------------------------------------------------------------
rem DO NOT EDIT THIS FILE WHILE IT IS RUNNING. NOT EVEN A COMMENT.
rem
rem cmd.exe reads a batch file INCREMENTALLY, BY BYTE OFFSET, as it executes
rem it. Changing the file's length mid-run moves everything after the cursor,
rem and execution resumes at an offset that no longer means what it meant.
rem
rem That cost INFRA-VIEWER-001 a four-hour qualification that had PASSED: two
rem minutes in, a comment was reworded; four hours later, when qualify.cmd
rem returned, cmd.exe resumed at a stale offset and called it a SECOND time,
rem truncating qualification-times.txt and overwriting three of debug-ext's
rem logs. The run had already printed "every stage exited 0" and the evidence
rem for it was gone.
rem
rem EVERY LINE OF THIS FILE BEGINS WITH rem, set, call, echo, setlocal,
rem endlocal OR @echo FOLLOWED BY A SPACE OR THE END OF THE LINE, AND THAT IS
rem CHECKED BEFORE THE RUN BY A WHOLE-WORD MATCH. P19-ARCH-001's copy had a
rem line beginning "remrem" that a prefix match let through; cmd ran it as a
rem command and printed "not recognized" to stderr. P19-FLUID-001 fixed the
rem line and the check, and the check caught the same splice once more.
rem ---------------------------------------------------------------------
rem
rem P19-MESH-001 CFD MESH CONTRACT. The exact invocation, recorded so the run
rem is reproducible rather than described.
rem
rem qualify.cmd is byte-identical to the one P16-SIZE-001 settled on and every
rem milestone since has used, FIFTY-FOUR in a row counting this one.
rem
rem   qualify.cmd          git hash-object d313a64070718c44fae290ac042fe259d1a03c8b
rem   verify-harness.cmd   git hash-object 11855b8ff891093b021d1e0351761283d0eedd24
rem   launch.cmd           git hash-object f11039e6dc366d7c469a15cf74fb3867fd5ffeff
rem
rem CMAKE_BUILD_PARALLEL_LEVEL=6, carried for the reason INFRA-VIEWER-001
rem recorded: a CLEAN build of over 600 template-heavy translation units at full
rem parallelism exhausted the commit charge. ctest stays at -j 8.
rem
rem WHAT THIS MILESTONE ADDS. cfd gains the CFD mesh contract (CfdMesh.hpp and
rem .cpp): a face census of the P16 Tet4 mesh, nine named refusals and a
rem stamp-bound proof, staged after the input boundary (ADR-063). No other
rem module changes, so only cfd and the test executable recompile beyond the
rem clean every preset does anyway.
rem
rem What IS in the repeat set, and why. unit.Cfd the CFD cases, the new CfdMesh
rem cases among them; unit.Mesh, unit.Volume, unit.Tet and unit.Siz the P16
rem suites whose meshes the gate inspects; unit.ReferenceModel the reference
rem bodies it runs on; unit.Fluid, unit.Thermal and unit.Structural the sibling
rem consumers of the same mesh boundary; the rest as before. compile_fail is
rem excluded from the REPEAT (each case is a real compilation); it is in the
rem full ctest of every preset.
rem
rem QUALIFY_REPEAT is expanded as !REPEAT! inside qualify.cmd, never %REPEAT%:
rem a %VAR% holding | ( or ) is substituted when the for-block is PARSED and
rem closes the block early, killing the run after every preset has passed.
rem
rem THIS RUN HAPPENS ON THE HASIB MACHINE, as every milestone since P17-CLI-001,
rem by the owner's decision of 2026-10-14. GCC 16.1.0 WinLibs POSIX UCRT r4,
rem the CMake 4.4.1 and Ninja it bundles, and the dependency prefix built by
rem deps/CMakeLists.txt from the same hash-verified archives: Qt 6.11.2, OCCT
rem 8.0.1, zlib 1.3.1, Netgen 6.2.2604. The machine-specific cache values
rem (build root, dependency prefix, FetchContent source directories) were
rem configured for P17-CLI-001; qualify.cmd's plain `cmake --preset` reuses them.
rem
rem BEFORE LAUNCHING, the OneDrive client is restarted and its memory checked:
rem P19-ARCH-001's first attempt lost its debug link to a OneDrive process
rem holding 56 GB.
rem
rem AND NOW THE DISK IS CHECKED TOO. That ritual covers commit charge and not
rem disk, which is what attempt 1 of this milestone died of: %TEMP% filled, all
rem three builds aborted writing cc*.s, five of seventeen stages failed and no
rem suite ran. preflight-space.cmd measures the %TEMP% volume and the build-root
rem volume, refuses below QUALIFY_MIN_FREE_GB, and ends the process rather than
rem reaching the qualify.cmd line below. The check is a separate pair of files
rem because a comparison cannot live in THIS file: `if` is not one of the
rem allowed line prefixes, and qualify.cmd is byte-identical across fifty-four
rem milestones and is not this milestone's to touch.
rem
rem QUALIFY_MIN_FREE_GB IS SET BELOW TO 20, FROM A MEASUREMENT, chosen by the
rem owner on 2026-10-30. The preflight refuses below it on EACH distinct volume --
rem the %TEMP% volume and the build-root volume, counted once when they are one.
rem
rem How 20 was arrived at, recorded in full in FREEZE.md: the three presets were
rem built from an EMPTY build root on the second machine and measured at 11 495 MB
rem (11.23 GB) with the GUI off, plus a 7.4 MB peak of %TEMP% compiler scratch at
rem -j6, about 4 MB of ctest artifacts per tree, and about 149 MB for the GUI this
rem machine cannot build (Qt DLL staging for three trees plus the three app
rem binaries). About 12 GB from empty, so 20 leaves about 8 GB free at the end.
rem
rem This script's own advice -- calibrate from the last passing run with
rem
rem     powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File preflight-space.ps1 -WithSizes
rem
rem -- could NOT be followed, and that is why the figure was measured instead:
rem P19-FLUID-001's freeze records COMMIT CHARGE (18.1 GB down to 0.08 GB), not
rem disk free space, so no passing run has ever left a measured disk figure.
rem
rem 20 is a floor, not a forecast, and it is deliberately generous: if the previous
rem run's trees are still present the run is close to net-zero on disk, because
rem qualify.cmd's :clean runs `ninja -t clean` on a preset immediately before
rem rebuilding that same preset, freeing its outputs before writing new ones.
rem
rem THE FRESHNESS HALF of the fresh-binary proof (the binaries are newer than
rem the clean and than the newest source) is done by postrun-mesh.ps1, after
rem the run.
setlocal
set "BETTERCAD_BUILD_ROOT=C:/Users/hasib/bcdev/bc-build"
set "CMAKE_BUILD_PARALLEL_LEVEL=6"
set "QUALIFY_PRESETS=debug-ext release-ext debug-shared-ext"
set "QUALIFY_REPEAT_PRESETS=release-ext debug-ext"
set "QUALIFY_MIN_FREE_GB=20"
set "QUALIFY_REPEAT=architecture|unit\.Linalg|unit\.Structural|unit\.Cfd|unit\.Fluid|unit\.Provenance|unit\.CustomMaterial|unit\.MaterialFile|unit\.MaterialCli|unit\.Thermal|unit\.P18Qualification|unit\.P17Qualification|unit\.Quality|unit\.MeshDofMap|unit\.ConstraintSet|unit\.FreeEquationMap|unit\.Tet4Element|unit\.Mesh|unit\.Volume|unit\.Tet|unit\.Siz|unit\.Id|unit\.ReferenceModel|unit\.Analytic|unit\.View|refmod\.|gui\.|cli\.thermal\.|cli\.structural\.|cli\.mesh\."
call "%~dp0preflight-space.cmd"
call "%~dp0qualify.cmd" "%~dp0."
set "RESULT=%errorlevel%"
echo qualify.cmd exit %RESULT%
endlocal & exit /b %RESULT%
